{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-11-11T10:12:40.665Z","type":"exp.start","exp":"E-HOSTED-FAILCLOSED-LIVE-01","attempt":1,"title":"The hosted Roost fails closed on real TDX hardware: with both escrow providers unreachable it refuses a charged round (503), keeps the bid and signs nothing","tier":"hardware","hypothesis":"Predictions are in docs/lab/PROGRAMME_PLAN.md, committed before this file existed. Inside a real confidential VM whose two providers can never resolve, a charged round is refused with 503 in bounded time, the sealed bid is still there afterwards, nothing can be signed, and retrying gives the same answer.","limits":["The first promoted run of this experiment (older build) sent an unsigned bid. On the signed-only compose that fails (run 20261111T094151Z-c01e, GAP-050); this version sends a signed bid from a throwaway account.","The providers are on the reserved .invalid domain, so this shows a total outage, not a partial one (partial failure is covered offline).","It does not show recovery: the providers are fixed in the VM's measured compose file, so recovery needs a second VM.","The compose file is a test fixture that differs from the real one only in the two escrow provider URLs; it is attested here but is not a deployment members should trust.","The account-check providers failing is covered by unit tests, not here. One operator controls the VM and the throwaway account (0.1 NEAR, deleted)."],"requires":["phala-key","near-key","network","docker"],"chain_prev":"93350d6330af0084040fca47de2b75c249d276cf9a6831f3d994e47ab0f630d6","chain_hash":"285d206c3663945d1b00a49ed2c047e0d2bdf8883b85f0b8d07d2b8b09d6d3a0"}
